              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is 46 mL/min/1.73m², which is within the reference range but at the lower end, indicating mildly to moderately reduced kidney function (CKD stage 3a). This is not unexpected in an 87-year-old and should be monitored, especially if there are comorbidities or nephrotoxic medications.</td></tr></table></div>"
